# BUILD A COMPLETE CIVIC COMPLAINT AGENT — AHMEDABAD MUNICIPAL CORPORATION DEMO

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, AI agent architect, UI/UX designer, and QA engineer. Build a complete, runnable, polished product named **CivicFlow AI — Intelligent Civic Complaint Assistant for Ahmedabad**.

Do not merely generate a landing page, wireframe, prototype, or static dashboard. Build a working end-to-end application with real image analysis through Gemini, real backend tool execution, persistent mock complaint records, complaint tracking, validation, error handling, and a professional user interface.

## 1. Core objective

Create an AI agent that helps citizens report:

- Potholes and damaged roads
- Garbage accumulation and overflowing bins
- Broken or malfunctioning streetlights
- Waterlogging and blocked stormwater drains

The citizen uploads a photograph, provides an area or location, reviews the AI analysis, and submits a complaint. The agent resolves the ward, identifies the responsible department, creates a complaint in a local mock AMC database, and returns a unique tracking ID.

The citizen can later enter the tracking ID or ask the agent a natural-language question such as:

- "What is the status of my complaint?"
- "Show my complaint details."
- "Which department is handling AMC-2026-000124?"
- "Where was this complaint registered?"

The status must be retrieved from the actual saved database record, never invented by the LLM.

This is a demonstration system, not an official Ahmedabad Municipal Corporation service. Clearly disclose this in the UI. Never claim that a complaint was submitted to the real AMC.

